sit - suckless iptv
===================
sit is a small IPTV player. It lists the live channels, movies and series
of an Xtream Codes account, shows the programme guide, and plays
everything through libmpv in one window. It is configured by editing
config.h and recompiling.


Requirements
------------
SDL2, libmpv, libcurl and an OpenGL 3.3 driver.

Debian, Ubuntu:

    apt install build-essential pkg-config \
                libsdl2-dev libmpv-dev libcurl4-openssl-dev

Arch:

    pacman -S base-devel sdl2 mpv curl

Other distributions: a C compiler, make, pkg-config and the development
packages of SDL2, libmpv and libcurl.

Windows: install MSYS2 (https://www.msys2.org) and, in its UCRT64 shell:

    pacman -S make mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gcc mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-pkgconf \
              mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-SDL2 mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-mpv


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your setup (sit is installed into /usr/local by
default), then, on Linux:

    make
    make install    (as root)

On Windows, in the UCRT64 shell:

    make OS=win


Running sit
-----------
    sit [-v] [-s sources] [url ...]

On Windows, start it from the UCRT64 shell (./sit.exe), or put
C:\msys64\ucrt64\bin on PATH, or copy the DLLs it needs next to it:

    ldd sit.exe | awk '/ucrt64/ { print $3 }' | xargs -I{} cp {} .

Without sources sit shows a few public test streams. URLs given on the
command line are listed as a source of their own.


Sources
-------
One line per provider, fields separated by tabs:

    Home	xtream	http://provider.example:8080	username	password

in ~/.config/sit/sources (Windows: %APPDATA%\sit\sources), or in a file
given with -s. Without such a file, sources[] in config.h is used.


Keys
----
    Enter       play; on what plays: full view
    Esc         back
    up, down    move (also k, j)
    left, right switch panes (also h, l); in full view: seek
    Tab         Live, Movies, Series, Favorites, Recent
    /           search
    f           favorite
    e           guide; Enter on a past programme plays its recording
    Space       pause
    [ ]         previous, next channel
    a s         audio, subtitle track
    - = m       volume down, up, mute
    r           refresh the list
    Alt+1..9    switch source
    F11         fullscreen
    q           quit


Configuration
-------------
The configuration of sit is done by creating a custom config.h and
(re)compiling the source code. make creates config.h from config.def.h
on the first build. Fonts, colours, sizes, keys, mpv options and cache
times are there.


Files
-----
    ~/.config/sit/sources       providers
    ~/.cache/sit/               lists, guides and posters; safe to delete
    ~/.local/share/sit/         resume positions, favorites, recent

On Windows the first is %APPDATA%\sit, the cache %LOCALAPPDATA%\sit and
the rest %APPDATA%\sit.
